{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you tonight. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I was in a car accident two days ago. A car ran a red light and hit me head-on. The airbag went off, and I blacked out for a second."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Did you go to the ER then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I drove myself. They did a CT scan and said no bleeding in my head or broken neck. I had a burn on my left wrist from the airbag. They sent me home with pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And since then, what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My headache got worse. It’s in my forehead, really bad, and I started vomiting—yellow fluid, not bloody. I couldn’t keep anything down, not even water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds rough. And you said you couldn’t take your medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No. I haven’t taken my prednisone, Florinef, or Synthroid since the accident. I just couldn’t keep them down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. You have Addison’s disease, so missing those steroid doses can be dangerous. We’ll get you back on them safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried about that. My PCP told me to come back to the ER, so I did."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good call. We’ve started you on IV fluids and gave you some Dilaudid for the pain. How’s the headache now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better since the medicine, but it still hurts a lot. It’s worse with light and noise. I had to ask for earplugs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds like a migraine. Given the accident, it could also be a post-concussion headache. But your repeat CT was clean, so no bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had migraines before, years ago. This feels similar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also gave you an injection of hydrocortisone to cover your Addison’s. You’ll get another dose soon, then switch back to your oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better. But the Dilaudid gives me the creeps—like I’m jittery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2164-07-20 03:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll note that. We can try other pain meds as your nausea improves. For now, we’re also giving Zofran for nausea through the IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2164-07-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2164-07-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Headache’s still there, but maybe a bit less. I haven’t vomited since last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2164-07-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’re going to keep you on IV fluids and slowly see if you can start drinking. Maybe some clear liquids later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2164-07-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like that. I’m really thirsty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2164-07-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray and ECG this morning—both normal. No heart or lung issues from the accident."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2164-07-20 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I was worried about that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2164-07-20 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back—electrolytes are stable, kidney function is good, and your blood count is where it usually is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2164-07-20 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s really wrong besides the headache and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2164-07-20 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your exam is normal, no signs of infection or abdominal issues. We think it’s migraine-related, worsened by stress and missing your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2164-07-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My neck is still stiff. And I had a muscle spasm earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2164-07-20 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s common after a crash. The neck tenderness is likely from muscle strain. We can add something mild for spasms if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2164-07-20 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been able to sip water and ginger ale without vomiting. That’s great. We’re switching you to oral anti-nausea meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2164-07-20 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel like I might actually eat something soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2164-07-20 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re now on your regular prednisone and Florinef by mouth. We’ll stop the IV steroids. Your blood pressure is stable—good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2164-07-20 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I’m back on my meds. I was scared I’d get an adrenal crisis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2164-07-20 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did the right thing coming in. Missing those doses with vomiting is risky. But you’re back on track now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you slept through the night, no vomiting, and you ate toast and applesauce. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great. But what if the headache comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home with your regular migraine meds. If the headache returns, try your usual routine. Use acetaminophen at night if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—should I keep taking them all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly as before. We’re increasing your Celexa to 20 mg for depression. And keep using the hydrocortisone injection if you’re sick or can’t take pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And when should I worry enough to come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your headache gets worse, or you have vision changes, weakness, fever, or can’t keep fluids down, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2164-07-21 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2164-07-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You can go home in a couple of hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2164-07-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home and rest in a quiet room."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2164-07-21 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check—you’re tolerating food, walking fine, and your pain is manageable. All set for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2164-07-21 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I was really scared, but you’ve helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2164-07-21 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy, follow up with your PCP, and call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2164-07-20 02:44:00",
    "admission_end": "2164-07-21 12:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of Addison’s disease and hypothyroidism, was admitted after a motor vehicle accident two days prior, during which she briefly lost consciousness and sustained a minor wrist burn. She developed a persistent bifrontal headache with photophobia, phonophobia, and vomiting, preventing her from taking her home steroid and thyroid medications. She was treated with IV fluids, IV hydrocortisone for adrenal coverage, and IV pain and anti-nausea medications. Her symptoms improved rapidly, and she was restarted on oral prednisone, Florinef, and Synthroid. Neurologic exams and repeat imaging were normal, supporting a diagnosis of migraine and post-concussion headache. She tolerated a regular diet, ambulated without issue, and was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to resume her baseline medications and monitor for worsening symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Migraine without aura, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Spasm of muscle",
      "Other motor vehicle traffic accident involving collision with motor vehicle injuring driver of motor vehicle other than motorcycle",
      "Street and highway accidents",
      "Glucocorticoid deficiency",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
